  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The render law",
      "items": [
        "config.json is fully generated from the roster — hand-edits are overwritten",
        "kit apply is the only writer; dashboard saves go back through the kit CLI",
        "idempotent: unchanged files stay byte-identical; config backed up before write",
        "every path is machine-local — the router listens on 127.0.0.1 only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Keys & provider config",
      "items": [
        "roster carries env-var names only; values live in ~/.zcode/router/.env (chmod 600)",
        "provider_config.json is schemaVersion-guarded: the kit rewrites only its own keys, backup + re-parse verify first",
        "a key is trusted until a real use of it is refused (401, or 403 speaking key vocabulary)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Failure laws",
      "items": [
        "usage-limit vocabulary is classified before 429 — a plan's window is quota, even when phrased as rate limiting",
        "quota, billing and rate-limit bodies never blame the key; benches: quota 30 min, rate 5 min",
        "parity: fallbacks declaring images/tools false are excluded from the chain before quota steering"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Workflow plane",
      "items": [
        "the plane is the engine edition's package by file: symlink — 16 modules, 0 deps",
        "kit apply ships it beside the router from the package's own exports + a node_modules link",
        "check:port asserts the kit and the installed runtime cannot drift from the engine"
      ]
    }
  ]
